# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Adam Lahouari et al. (2026). MolCryst-MLIPs: A Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials Database for Molecular Crystals.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.6c00735  arXiv:2604.13897v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2604.13897v2 (sha256 1756eed459c83575...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 248 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/lahouari2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the nine MACE models fine-tuned from MACE-MH-1 (omol head)
# for the molecular crystals of the MolCryst-MLIPs database, with their
# validation MAEs (Table 2), and their PBE-D4 training data built with AMLP.
# Lattice-energy ranking metrics against foundation models (Table 3),
# structural agreement (Table 4) and MD stability are not energy or force
# errors of the schema and are not encoded.

